    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="80">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 80</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="366" ed="#liebermann"/>And ic wylle, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc man si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_80.lnote.oe.5-2"/> his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda ⁊ on felda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_80.lnote.oe.6"/> on his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="366" ed="#liebermann"/>Be huntnaðe. And ic wylle, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc man sy his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda ⁊ on felda on his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="366" ed="#liebermann"/>And ic wille, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc man sy his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda ⁊ on fealda on his agana<hi rend="italic">n</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_80.lnote.oe.4"/><pb n="367" ed="#liebermann"/>Uolo, ut omnis homo sit uenatione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_80.lnote.oe.5"/> sua dignus in nemore et in campo in dominio suo.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="367" ed="#liebermann"/>Uolo etiam, ut omnis homo habeat uenationem suam in siluis et in planis super sua.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="367" ed="#liebermann"/>[U]olo etiam, ut omnis homo sua uenacione dignus sit tam in siluis quam in campis in suo proprio.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="80" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="214" ed="#robertson"/>Be huntnaðe. And ic wylle þæt ælc man sy his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda ⁊ on felda on his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="296" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ic wylle þæt ælc man si his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda and on felda on his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="366" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von Jagd. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und ich<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_80.lnote.de.1"/> will, das jedermann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_80.lnote.de.2"/> seiner Jagd theilhaftig sei in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_80.lnote.de.3"/> Wald und Feld auf seinem Eigen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of hunting. B) And I will that every man be entitled to his hunting in wood and field on his own land.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="215" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning hunting. And it is my will that every man shall be entitled to hunt in the woods and fields on his own property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="474" ed="#whitelock"/>And it is my will that every man is to be entitled to his hunting in wood and field on his own land.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="297" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And it is my desire that each person be entitled to hunt in his own woods and fields.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_4-2">CHn cor 4.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_5">CHn cor 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_6">CHn cor 6</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_6-1">CHn cor 6.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_7">CHn cor 7</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_9">CHn cor 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_10">CHn cor 10</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_11">CHn cor 11</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_12">CHn cor 12</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_13">CHn cor 13</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 367, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Be huntnaðe</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_80.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nolo <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Nolo Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_80.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor</hi> 80—81 <hi rend="italic">setzt</hi> 82 <hi rend="italic">DmTRHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">82 placed before 80—81 by DmTRHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_80.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">367</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nis sue <hi rend="italic">KL Angl.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nis sue KL Angl.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_80.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sẏ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sẏ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_80.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">366</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fealda <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fealda Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_80.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt aus Q durch Lond ECf 32 B 5, aus Inst durch Ps Cn for 30 mit der Einschränkung, nur der Adlige sei zur Jagd privilegiert und dem König Hochjagd vorbehalten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used, from Q, by Lond ECf 32 B 5, and, from Inst, by Ps Cn for 30, with the restriction that only the nobleman is privileged to hunt and that the hunting of big game is reserved to the king</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_80.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Forst 3a. 4. 6f.; Jagd 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Forst 3a. 4. 6f.; Jagd 9</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_80.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Formel häufig in Urkk. XI. Jhs.: Thorpe <hi rend="italic">Dipl</hi>. 369. 566. 593</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">A formula frequent in charters of the 11th cent.: Thorpe <hi rend="italic">Dipl</hi>. 369. 566. 593</seg></note>
      </div>
